implementationPlan.description:
Docs only: docs/MCP_SERVER.md, inside `### moe.release_task` (:2076-2135 at 6fbdc22f), with your own Edit tool. Never use a shell write or a subagent edit (global rail 3). The byte-exact prototype is in /mnt/d/moe-scratch/47652916-plan/proto-release_task.diff.
(a) Parameters block: insert two lines right AFTER the `workerId?: string, ...` line and BEFORE `force?: boolean`. This keeps `force` the last field, so its line, which has no trailing comma, stays untouched:
  `attemptId?: string,             // Optional fencing identity (≤128 chars): the attemptId moe.claim_next_task returned. Omitted = unfenced, as before`
  `generation?: number,            // Optional fencing token (integer ≥ 1): the generation moe.claim_next_task returned, checked together with attemptId`
(b) Add one paragraph right before the section's **Returns:** line. It starts "**Attempt fence.**" and says:
  - a presented attemptId (plus generation when supplied) goes through the step tools' currency check (assertAttemptCurrent), inside the state lock beside the ownership gates and before any write;
  - it must equal the task's current open attempt;
  - a superseded, closed or future attempt is refused `STATE_CONFLICT` (`-32002`) `ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED` and nothing is released;
  - a malformed identity (a blank or non-string attemptId, one over 128 characters, or a generation that is not a positive integer) is refused `INVALID_INPUT` (`-32602`);
  - a task with no attempt record skips the check, and an omitted identity is the unfenced legacy path;
  - the launchers' seat-outage release (`launch_outage_release`, `Invoke-MoeLaunchOutageRelease`) sends the pinned `MOE_ATTEMPT_ID` and `MOE_ATTEMPT_GENERATION`.
These facts come from releaseTask.ts:116-126, :168-170 and :219-224, util/enforcement.ts:137-158 and :183-230, and scripts/moe-agent.sh:9077-9103. Re-read them before writing. Edit nothing outside this section. Error handling: re-grep both anchors first; if a peer moved them, keep the same placement relative to `workerId?` and **Returns:**.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
docs/MCP_SERVER.md's `### moe.release_task` documents what the code already enforces:
- the optional attemptId and generation inputs;
- their currency check before any write, refused STATE_CONFLICT ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED;
- the malformed-identity INVALID_INPUT;
- the unfenced legacy path when the identity is omitted.
Docs only; no code changes.
